<!-- QUALITY TIERS -->
<section class="section section-alt" id="tiers">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <h2>Quality tiers, not vendor lock-in</h2>
      <p>
        Declare <code>quality: high</code> and the tool tries the tier ladder in order,
        grading against your eval block and falling back on failure. The ladders — and the
        default model per service — live in a runtime YAML config you can override without
        rebuilding the binary.
      </p>
      <p>
        Async providers (Veo, Wan, Grok video, Suno) poll their tasks to completion; sync
        providers return directly. Long-running batches fan out across zellij panes with
        <code>-j</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="code-panel">
{%raw}<pre><code><span class="c"># media-tool.yaml (runtime override)</span>
defaults:
  gemini: gemini-3.1-flash-image

image_tiers:
  medium:
    - gemini:gemini-3.1-flash-image
    - gemini:gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image
    - qwen-image:qwen-image-3.0
  high:
    - gemini:gemini-3-pro-image
    - gemini:gemini-3.1-flash-image
    - qwen-image:qwen-image-3.0-pro

refine_model: gemini-3.7-flash</code></pre>{/raw}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- PROVIDER OPTIONS -->
<section class="section" id="options">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Escape hatches when you need them</h2>
    <div class="benefit-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Pin the service</h3>
        <p>
          <code>service:</code> plus optional <code>model:</code> bypass auto-selection —
          useful when a specific vendor's edit is required for an asset.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Pass provider options</h3>
        <p>
          <code>prompt.provider_options</code> carries provider-specific parameters —
          safety filter levels, token limits, temperature — without polluting the prompt
          text.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Override per invocation</h3>
        <p>
          CLI flags <code>--service</code>, <code>--model</code>, and
          <code>--quality</code> override any prompt file at runtime — handy for A/B-ing a
          tier against the same asset.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-row center">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/extensibility">Adding your own provider</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
